/**
\page cmdDraw Draw Menu

\anchor idx_Draw_Menu_111

<i>Draw</i> commands are used to draw lines, arcs and other shapes. These can be used to represent water edges, bridges and other scenic features.

![](bdraw.png)

There are 4 command buttons on the tool-bar used to draw Straight Objects, Curved Lines, Circles and other Shapes.  Each command button is followed by a button that changes the action (and Icon) on the command button.

![](mdraw.png)

Functions for drawing basic shapes and objects like lines and curves can be accessed from this menu.

- <b>Circle Lines</b> - draw empty or filled circles. (\ref cmdDrawCircles)

- <b>Curved Lines</b> - are created in the same manner as curved tracks. (\ref cmdDrawCurves)

- <b>Note</b> - attach a note icon to a specific location on the layout. (\ref cmdNote)

- <b>Ruler</b> - create ruler and set visibility (\ref cmdRuler)

- <b>Protractor</b> - create protractor and set visibility (\ref cmdAngle)

- <b>Shapes</b> - draw boxes, polygons and poly-lines. (\ref cmdDrawShapes)

- <b>Straight Objects</b> - draw straight objects. (\ref cmdDrawStraight)

- <b>Text</b> - allows entry of text directly onto the layout. (\ref cmdText)

Some commands display controls on the Status Line (\ref mainW) to change line width, color or other attributes of the object.

- \subpage cmdDrawCircles
- \subpage cmdDrawCurves
- \subpage cmdNote
- \subpage cmdRuler
- \subpage cmdAngle
- \subpage cmdDrawShapes
- \subpage cmdDrawStraights
- \subpage DrawOrigin
- \subpage cmdText

*/

/**
\page cmdDrawCircles Circles and Filled Circles

\anchor idx_Circles_and_Filled_Circles_112

![](mdrawcircles.png)

Before a Circle is drawn its line width and color can be set. For Filled Circles, the color can be set.
The <b>Circle Line Width</b> field is a scaled dimension in inches if &gt;0. If 0 it is a 1 pixel wide line at all zooms. If the value is negative, it is a scale-independent number of pixels wide.

<b>Circles</b> and <b>Filled Circles</b> are created by selecting either the center position or a point on the edge of the circle and dragging to specify the radius.

- \ref cmdDrawCircleTangent. Draw a Circle from the Edge.

- \ref cmdDrawCircleCenter. Draw a Circle from the Center.

- \ref cmdDrawFilledCircleTangent. Draw a Filled Circle from the Edge.

- \ref cmdDrawFilledCircleCenter. Draw a Filled Circle from the Center.

- \subpage cmdDrawCircleTangent
- \subpage cmdDrawCircleCenter
- \subpage cmdDrawFilledCircleTangent
- \subpage cmdDrawFilledCircleCenter

*/

